{
 "_comment": [
  "Brainrot meshes, by character id.",
  "",
  "native = the mesh's TRUE intrinsic size, read from",
  "AssetService:CreateMeshPartAsync(meshId).Size -- NOT the Size of any MeshPart",
  "that happens to use it. That distinction is the whole reason this line exists:",
  "the pack's models scale their meshes down via Size, and recording that scaled",
  "value made every brainrot render hundreds of times too large. A MeshPart shows",
  "its mesh at Size/InitialSize, so declaring InitialSize smaller than the mesh",
  "really is inflates it by exactly that ratio -- 475x for tralalero_tralala.",
  "",
  "The pack mixes scales: most meshes are 400-2048 studs, a few (meowl, w_or_l,",
  "1x1x1x1) are single digits. So every entry is measured, never inferred.",
  "",
  "These are baked into ReplicatedStorage.BrainrotModels by tools/build_place.py.",
  "They CANNOT be applied at runtime: MeshPart.MeshId and TextureID are not",
  "writable from a script, so every part has to already exist and be cloned.",
  "",
  "native  = the size the source reported for the raw asset.",
  "target  = what the model's LARGEST dimension should become on a pad.",
  "          Largest-dimension rather than height, because these come in all",
  "          shapes and normalising a flat wide one to a standard height",
  "          leaves it enormous across.",
  "",
  "`variants` holds a per-variant TEXTURE for the same mesh. Measured across",
  "the pack: geometry is identical for all 435 variant models and only the",
  "texture changes, so a variant is a retexture and costs one extra MeshPart",
  "rather than a second copy of the geometry.",
  "",
  "Not every variant is here. Rainbow ships untextured in the pack -- it is a",
  "plain mesh plus a rainbow ParticleEmitter -- and Frost has no pack art at",
  "all. Both keep the older SHELL treatment: a tinted, slightly enlarged,",
  "semi-transparent copy of the mesh over the textured original. That is why",
  "entries still emit BodyPlain alongside Body.",
  "",
  "Characters the pack does not cover keep their generated mesh and have no",
  "`variants`, so they fall through to the shell for every variant."
 ],
